{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_346c739218c44b04977a6e04","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":".\n- dark-factory:generate-prompts-for-spec: Generate dark-factory prompt files from an approved spec. This command runs the generation workflow to create executable prompt files from an approved specification. The YOLO container uses the generated prompt files to build the feature. This command is not interactive.\n- dark-factory:run-prompt: Execute prompt directly in YOLO container (simplified for one-shot headless execution).\n- dark-factory:watch: Watch dark-factory progress with sound alerts for completion, and stuck prompts.\n- dark-factory:read-guides: All dark-factory guides.\n- dark-factory:audit-spec: Audit spec file against preflight checklist and quality criteria\n- dark-factory:adjust-priority: Adjust priority of the current executing or queued prompt\n- dark-factory:init-project: Initialize a project for self-hosting dark-factory on a standalone project, using built-in services.\n- dark-factory:create-spec: Create a new spec file, writes to specs/in-progress/.\n- dark-factory:create-prompt: Create a new prompt file, written to prompts/in-progress/.\n- dark-factory:run: One-shot dark-factory run — run all queued prompts. Takes as the primary arg the directory to operate on (defaults to current directory). Also accepts args such as sessions, prompts in order. Outputs regular status updates and logs in /dark-factory/status.\n- dark-factory:create-scenario: Run scenario file from an earlier prompt, requires a scenario from create-scenario.\n- dark-factory:spec-proposal: Start a management-session-driven proposal flow to write and refine a spec, including an approve step in the management session.\n- dark-factory:verify-spec: Walk a dark-factory spec through real end-to-end verification, then update its status and use the CLI to mark complete.\n- dark-factory:guide-picker: All dark-factory guides with their skill files. For finding the right guide for a specific task, use prompt-writing and scenario-guide. The audit skills (audit-spec, audit-prompt, audit-scenario) can be used to validate generated files.\n\nLet me start by reading the referenced files.\n\nLet me read the key files:\n1. `scripts/sentry-read.sh` — the script under test\n2. `scripts/sentry-create-tasks.sh` — for style\n3. `specs/in-progress/001-sentry-read-event-payload.md` — for the contract\n\nLet me start.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c729a40-9f17-48f3-962d-d97a743f243d","uuid":"2fbf7cf6-40f4-4b19-8694-998ec396ed1e","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:44:23.314Z"}
