{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_3cfb236e56524ad7943529bc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" The container has `HTTP_PROXY`/`http_proxy`/`HTTPS_PROXY`/`https_proxy` set. curl honors these and routes even localhost requests through tinyproxy, which filters them (403).\n\nThe fix for the harness: export `NO_PROXY`/`no_proxy` to include `127.0.0.1` and `localhost`. curl checks `no_proxy`/`NO_PROXY` and bypasses the proxy for matching hosts. Since the fixture server is on `127.0.0.1:<port>`, setting `NO_PROXY=127.0.0.1,localhost` will make curl connect directly.\n\nThis is a test-environment concern — legitimate to set in the harness. It doesn't modify sentry-read.sh. And it's harmless in environments without a proxy.\n\nLet me verify that NO_PROXY fixes it first, then add to the harness.\n\nLet me test:\n```\nNO_PROXY=127.0.0.1,localhost HTTP_PROXY=... curl ...\n```\n\nActually let me just test with the env set.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c729a40-9f17-48f3-962d-d97a743f243d","uuid":"7549a8c5-e3f2-42ca-a566-96778a08fc24","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:45:46.563Z"}
